   "etymology": "From Proto-Albanian *tˢ́ika, from Pre-Proto-Albanian *ćīkā ~ *ćeykā, from Proto-Indo-European *ḱeh₃- (“to sharpen”). A PPA form *ćīkā supports a Proto-Indo-European *k̑iH-keh2- form, while *ćeykā supports a Proto-Indo-European *k̑éi̯H-keh2- form. The absence of an a-umlaut favors against a short -i- in *ćikā, which was posited by Orel.\nAlternatively, Meyer considers a borrowing from Latin sīca (“a poniard, curved dagger”), while other scholars believe instead the opposite.",
